I've just uploaded a new copy of Slycrel -- version 2.51.  Its file name is "Slycrel 2.51.sit".  This version is a major overhaul including the following additions:+ All three externals have now been converted to C/C++ so I don't have to   look at PASCAL (gag!... especially THINK PASCAL) all the time, having   flashbacks to my college days.  This should make programming and   debugging much easier in the future since support for PASCAL isn't so   good anymore.+ Added C++ error checking to make program errors quit the external more   gracefully.+ Performed a general cleanup of the code to help with tracking down   errors.+ Added new monster, armor, and weapon names rather than using a "Default"   name.+ Added code for all formerly dimmed out menu selections.+ Added new text strings to monster text combat section.  This part of   the external only used to partially work, and quite often would print   out a "-- Blank --" string.+ Sly Terrain Editor:  Selecting which terrain file to edit is now done   by menu selection.+ SlySysOp Editor: Selecting which player to edit is now done by menu   selection.+ Fixed too many other small bugs to mention.Thanks to those who have made suggestions to help improve Slycrel.  Ifyou have any problems, or you'd like to make some suggestions, pleasefeel free to email me here on Olympus or on the internet at ddolinar@utw.com. - Bill